```cpp
// Camera node
Node* cameraNode = scene_->CreateChild("Camera");
cameraNode->SetPosition(Vector3(0.0f, 10.0f, -20.0f));
cameraNode->LookAt(Vector3::ZERO);

// Camera component
auto* camera = cameraNode->CreateComponent<Camera>();
camera->SetFarClip(500.0f);
camera->SetFov(45.0f);

// Viewport connects scene + camera to screen
auto* renderer = GetSubsystem<Renderer>();
SharedPtr<Viewport> viewport(new Viewport(context_, scene_, camera));
renderer->SetViewport(0, viewport);
```

Note: Camera is a Component attached to a Node. The Node's transform controls where the camera is and what it looks at. Viewport is NOT a component — it's created with new and set on the Renderer subsystem.

```cpp
auto* cache = GetSubsystem<ResourceCache>();

// Create node at the sound position
Node* soundNode = scene_->CreateChild("HitSound");
soundNode->SetPosition(Vector3(10.0f, 1.0f, 5.0f));

// Add 3D sound source
auto* source = soundNode->CreateComponent<SoundSource3D>();
source->SetNearDistance(2.0f);
source->SetFarDistance(50.0f);

// Load and play
auto* sound = cache->GetResource<Sound>("Sounds/Hit.wav");
source->Play(sound);

// IMPORTANT: camera node needs SoundListener
cameraNode_->CreateComponent<SoundListener>();
GetSubsystem<Audio>()->SetListener(
    cameraNode_->GetComponent<SoundListener>());
```

Without SoundListener on the camera, 3D audio has no reference point and you hear nothing. Common mistake.

```cpp
// Subscribe in Start()
SubscribeToEvent(E_KEYDOWN, URHO3D_HANDLER(MyApp, HandleKeyDown));

// Handler
void MyApp::HandleKeyDown(StringHash eventType, VariantMap& eventData)
{
    using namespace KeyDown;
    int key = eventData[P_KEY].GetInt();

    if (key == KEY_ESCAPE)
        engine_->Exit();
    else if (key == KEY_F1)
        GetSubsystem<Console>()->Toggle();
    else if (key == KEY_F2)
        GetSubsystem<DebugHud>()->ToggleAll();
}
```

Handler signature is ALWAYS: void ClassName::MethodName(StringHash eventType, VariantMap& eventData)
Never float, never EventData*, never any other signature.
P_KEY gives the logical key code (KEY_ESCAPE, KEY_W, KEY_SPACE, etc).

```cpp
void MyComponent::Update(float timeStep)
{
    // Get the node's forward direction from its rotation
    Vector3 forward = node_->GetRotation() * Vector3::FORWARD;

    // Move along that direction
    node_->Translate(forward * speed_ * timeStep, TS_WORLD);

    // Or simpler — Translate in local space (default)
    node_->Translate(Vector3::FORWARD * speed_ * timeStep);

    // Rotate (yaw around Y axis)
    node_->Rotate(Quaternion(0.0f, turnSpeed_ * timeStep, 0.0f));
}
```

Translate defaults to TS_LOCAL (relative to node's rotation). Use TS_WORLD for absolute movement. Vector3::FORWARD is (0, 0, 1) — Z forward in Urho3D's right-handed system.

Override OnNodeSet or the destructor:

```cpp
class MyComponent : public LogicComponent
{
    URHO3D_OBJECT(MyComponent, LogicComponent);
public:
    ~MyComponent() override
    {
        // Destructor cleanup
    }

protected:
    void OnNodeSet(Node* node) override
    {
        if (!node)  // Being removed from node
        {
            // Unsubscribe events, release resources
            UnsubscribeFromAllEvents();
        }
        else  // Being added to node
        {
            // Initialize
        }
    }
};
```

SharedPtr members auto-release when the component is destroyed. For manual cleanup (event unsubscription, external state), use OnNodeSet(nullptr) or the destructor.
